<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
    <string>$(DEVELOPMENT_LANGUAGE)</string>
    <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
    <string>Whoopsy</string>
    <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
    <string>$(EXECUTABLE_NAME)</string>
    <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
    <string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
    <key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
    <string>6.0</string>
    <key>CFBundleName</key>
    <string>$(PRODUCT_NAME)</string>
    <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
    <string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_PACKAGE_TYPE)</string>
    <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
    <string>1.0.0</string>
    <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
    <string>1</string>
    <key>LSRequiresIPhoneOS</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- The Mapbox PUBLIC token (`pk.…`), read by `MapboxSetup.configure()` and required for the
         offline route map — the `USE OFFLINE MAP` switch on the live session screen and the card it
         draws.

         **The key lives here; the token does not.** `MBXAccessToken` stays the one read path because
         it is Mapbox's own documented mechanism, but its value is expanded at build time from
         `MBX_ACCESS_TOKEN`, which two xcconfig files define: the committed
         `App/Config/Mapbox.xcconfig`, set as this target's base configuration in `Whoopsy.xcodeproj`
         (so it applies to Debug and Release alike) and defining the setting **empty**, and the
         **gitignored** `App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig` beside it, which the committed file pulls in
         through `#include?` when it exists and whose value therefore wins. The token lives only in the
         second file, so it is never committed.

         A clone that has not created `App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig` therefore gets a genuinely
         **empty** string here, not an unexpanded variable: `configure()` returns `false` and the build
         behaves exactly like `UnavailableOfflineMaps` — the switch is simply not offered and the card
         draws MapKit. Nothing is half-configured and nothing crashes.

         **The committed base file is not optional, and that is why the token is in the other one.**
         `xcodebuild` treats a base configuration it cannot open as a hard error —
         `Unable to open base configuration reference file` — and fails the build before compiling
         anything. A token file named as the base configuration would make every fresh clone
         unbuildable; `#include?` makes it merely unconfigured. Do not delete `Mapbox.xcconfig`, and do
         not merge the two files.

         This is NOT a secret: a public token ships inside every built app and Mapbox designs it to be
         embedded. The SECRET token (`sk.…`, with `Downloads:Read`) is a build-time credential for
         SwiftPM's package resolution and lives in `~/.netrc` — never here, never in either xcconfig,
         never anywhere in this tree. See README.md §Building. -->
    <key>MBXAccessToken</key>
    <string>$(MBX_ACCESS_TOKEN)</string>
    <key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Whoopsy requires Bluetooth access to discover, connect to, and stream biometrics from your WHOOP strap.</string>
    <key>NSBluetoothPeripheralUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Whoopsy requires Bluetooth access to communicate with your WHOOP strap.</string>
    <key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Whoopsy reads heart rate variability and resting heart rate from Apple Health to score Recovery. The import is processed on this device and never uploaded.</string>
    <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Whoopsy uses your location only while an active workout is recording to draw your route on the workout map.</string>
    <key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- NOT `NSSupportsLiveActivitiesFrequentUpdates`. That key is about *push*-driven updates arriving
         from a server, and this app has no server: every content update is pushed locally from a BLE
         callback through `LiveActivityController`. Declaring it would ask for a budget this app never
         spends, and the card's timer needs no update at all — it is system-rendered. -->
    <key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
    <array>
        <string>bluetooth-central</string>
        <!-- Required for `allowsBackgroundLocationUpdates` on `CoreLocationTrackingService`: setting
             that flag without this entry raises `NSInternalInconsistencyException` at launch rather
             than being ignored, so the two are a pair. Without it a route stops growing the moment
             the screen locks, which is most of a run. -->
        <string>location</string>
    </array>
    <key>UILaunchScreen</key>
    <dict/>
    <key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations</key>
    <array>
        <string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
